<!-- Minimal reproduction: a lyric word whose syllables are split across two voices
     of the same staff, as commonly engraved in closed-score (SATB) vocal music.
     Verse 1 sings "The ri-sing glo-ry": while voice 1 holds a whole note on "The",
     voice 2 carries the "ri" (begin) syllable; the "sing" (end) syllable is carried
     by the next voice-1 note. Without cross-voice re-linking no dash is drawn
     between "ri" and "sing". "glo-ry" stays within voice 1 as a control word; its "ry"
     is marked single, as some exporters write a last syllable, which still ends the word.
     The tenor (voice 5) sings the same words in the lower staff, in its own voice:
     its words are complete, and words are only re-linked within a staff. -->
